# Specification

> Iterative specification by feature group. Each section corresponds to one scenario.
> Updated incrementally after each implementation phase.

---

## Iteration 1 — Room Setup & Lobby (Scenario 1)

### Acceptance Criteria

| ID | Criterion | Detail |
|---|---|---|
| 1.1 | Host assignment | Room creator is stored as `hostId`. Snapshot exposes `hostId` to all participants. |
| 1.2 | Name validation | Names are trimmed on create/join. Empty or whitespace-only names rejected with `"Name cannot be empty"`. |
| 1.3 | Room code handling | Room codes are case-insensitive (uppercased server-side). Non-existent codes return 404. |
| 1.4 | Multi-room isolation | Each room is an independent `Map` entry. No data leaks between rooms. |
| 1.5 | Lobby auto-polling | Lobby polls `GET /rooms/:code` every ~2 seconds. Existing manual refresh button retained. |
| 1.6 | Start game gating | "Start Game" button visible only to host. Enabled only when ≥2 participants present. |
| 1.7 | Start game call | Clicking "Start Game" calls `POST /rooms/:code/start` before navigating to `/game`. |
| 1.8 | Host indicator | Lobby shows a visual indicator next to the host's name (e.g., "(Host)"). |

### Edge Cases
- Player creates room, then a second player joins — both see the lobby with correct host.
- Player enters a 4-char code that doesn't exist — error message shown, not redirected.
- Room with 1 participant — "Start Game" button is visible to host but disabled.

---

## Iteration 2 — Game Start & Drawer Flow (Scenario 2)

### Acceptance Criteria

| ID | Criterion | Detail |
|---|---|---|
| 2.1 | Name validation on join | Same as 1.2 — names trimmed, empty/whitespace rejected. |
| 2.2 | Drawer assignment | First player (host) is assigned role `"drawer"`. All other players are `"guesser"`. |
| 2.3 | Word selection | Secret word chosen deterministically: `wordIndex = participants.length % WORDS.length`. |
| 2.4 | Word visibility | `secretWord` field is non-null only in the drawer's snapshot. Null for guessers. |
| 2.5 | Role visibility | Each player sees their own role via `myRole` field in the snapshot. |
| 2.6 | Status transition | Start game transitions room from `"lobby"` to `"playing"`. |
| 2.7 | Start-game validation | Only host can start. Room must have ≥2 participants. Otherwise returns 403/400. |

### Edge Cases
- Non-host tries to start game — server returns 403, button not visible on frontend.
- Drawer sees the word in the UI; guessers see `"???"` or a hidden placeholder.
- Word index wraps correctly: 2 players → `words[2]`, 6 players → `words[1]`, etc.

---

## Iteration 3 — Gameplay Interaction (Scenario 3)

### Acceptance Criteria

| ID | Criterion | Detail |
|---|---|---|
| 3.1 | Canvas drawing | Drawer can draw via mouse on an HTML5 Canvas element. |
| 3.2 | Auto-save strokes | Each stroke is sent to `POST /rooms/:code/draw` on mouseup. |
| 3.3 | Canvas visibility | All players see current canvas strokes fetched via polling. |
| 3.4 | Clear canvas | Drawer has a "Clear Canvas" button. Calls `POST /rooms/:code/clear-drawing`. |
| 3.5 | Guess submission | Guessers can submit guesses via `POST /rooms/:code/guess`. |
| 3.6 | Guess validation | Guesses are trimmed. Empty/whitespace-only rejected with `"Guess cannot be empty"`. |
| 3.7 | Guess comparison | Case-insensitive: `guess.trim().toLowerCase() === secretWord`. |
| 3.8 | Score allocation | Correct guess: +100 points. Incorrect: +0 points. All scores start at 0 at game start. |
| 3.9 | Guess history | All guesses (player name, text, correct/incorrect) available in snapshot. |
| 3.10 | Synced history | All players see the full guess history via polling. |
| 3.11 | Role enforcement | Drawer cannot submit guesses (server rejects). Guessers cannot draw/clear (server rejects). |

### Edge Cases
- Drawer tries to open guess panel — hidden or disabled.
- Guesser tries to draw/clear — server returns 403, button disabled on frontend.
- Case mismatch: "Rocket", "ROCKET", "RoCkEt" all match "rocket".
- Whitespace: "  rocket  " is trimmed to "rocket" and matches.
- Multiple correct guesses after round ends — once status is "finished", new guesses rejected.

---

## Iteration 4 — Result, Restart & Final Validation (Scenario 4)

### Acceptance Criteria

| ID | Criterion | Detail |
|---|---|---|
| 4.1 | Round end trigger | When a guesser submits the correct word, room status transitions to `"finished"`. |
| 4.2 | Result visibility | All players see the correct word, final scores, and full guess history. |
| 4.3 | Secret word revealed | When status is `"finished"`, `secretWord` is visible to all players. |
| 4.4 | Restart button | "Play Again" button visible only to host when status is `"finished"`. |
| 4.5 | Restart action | Calls `POST /rooms/:code/restart`. Clears round state (word, drawer, scores, strokes, guesses). |
| 4.6 | Players preserved | Restart keeps all participants in the room. No one is removed. |
| 4.7 | Post-restart navigation | All players return to lobby (detected via polling — status changes back to `"lobby"`). |
| 4.8 | Full game flow | Two browsers can: create/join → lobby → start → drawer draws → guesser guesses → results → restart → lobby again. |

### Edge Cases
- Host restarts from finished state — all players see lobby again with participants intact.
- Player joins during "playing" or "finished" state — they see current state (no special handling beyond standard fetch).
- Round state is fully cleared: word, drawerId, scores reset, strokes cleared, guesses cleared.
